      "message": "\u003e While looking at pKVM-ARM code, seems it doesn\u0027t strictly use READ_ONCE for every read of the shared structures?\n\u003e\n\u003e  static void flush_hyp_vcpu(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu)\n\u003e  {\n\u003e     ...\n\nYeah, but maybe that\u0027s an oversight?\n\n@willdeacon@google.com @qperret@google.com @tabba@google.com in pKVM on ARM, do you strictly follow a rule to use READ_ONCE/WRITE_ONCE or similar primitives (rather than plain reads and writes) whenever reading or writing data from host\u0027s shared structures (`host_kvm`, `host_vcpu` etc)?\n\nAnd generally, what are your thoughts on this whole thread?",
