      "writtenOn": "2026-05-11T10:47:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You definitely need to use `READ_ONCE()` to avoid ToCToU issues but that doesn\u0027t mean you need to use it every time you access host-writable data. This stuff is really fiddly to get right and `flush_hyp_vcpu()` looks weird to me -- we probably  shouldn\u0027t care about `READ_ONCE()` for the non-protected case.",
